OK, I managed to compile module on Ubuntu 9.10. It's important that
you don't install libapreq2 from official repos, 'cause it comes
bundled with RApache. BUT, Debian/Ubuntu has very peculiar way of
loading/configuring Apache and its modules. Does anyone know how to
load compiled (not pre-compiled) module in Apache?

Compiled RApache module is located in /usr/lib/apache2/modules/
mod_R.so , now, how can I enable it, so Apache can see it?

