Hi all,

I'm trying to find time to update the main rapache.net <http://rapache.net> site, however I
always get distracted with work/life etc... so I'm calling on you guys
to see if anyone is interested in helping out. Here's a brief TODO
list which I'd like to set into action:

1. Re-design http://wiki.rapache.net/ site with new branding. I
splurged on a logo and web page design and I'd LOVE to see it up. If
you're interested in helping out, go to the wiki, register, and then
send me an email and I will make you a contributor for the site.
Currently, registration is open to anyone, but I've restricted updates
so the site won't be overrun by bots. All of the new branding and web
design assets are here in the attachment:
http://wiki.rapache.net/Main/NewPageDesign
2. Transfer all material on www.rapache.net <http://www.rapache.net> over to wiki.rapache.net <http://wiki.rapache.net>.
The biggest job will be changing the manual to a wiki topic so it's
easy to edit.
3. Switch over www.rapache.net <http://www.rapache.net> to wiki.rapache.net <http://wiki.rapache.net>
4. Set a direction to create new content on the site. I've created a
few presentations (although not very good) and they're scattered on
the internet. I've also played with creating screencast, so I'd be
happy to take your suggestions on what to put together.
5. Create an interface from the wiki to an rapache site so that people
can edit and run code in real-time! That will be fun!

Oh, according to the new branding I'm changing the casing of the
rapache name. It's now rApache!

Best,

Jeff
